@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af

title How public health data travels from a federal source to a person's screen

|Sources|
start
:fetch_all_sources
NPPES monthly dissemination, NPPES practice locations,
NUCC taxonomy, Census ZCTA-to-county, USDA RUCC,
F-105 specialty catalog;
:source_freshness_gate;
:source_archival
promotes each file to
{env}-pipeline-sources/{source}/{version}/;

|#f3f4f6|Atlas cluster ChatHealthyDataPipelines|
:load_staging_parallel
raw rows into the staging database;
:normalize_nucc, then publish_smd_and_embed
embeds every specialty with text-embedding-3-large;
:normalize_npi_per_state_fanout
add_secondary_practices
provider_flags_enrichment
harvest, classify and apply other identifier phrases
license_address_repair;
:county_enrichment
stamps fips, name and USDA RUCC 1-9
on every practice address;
:urban_flag
derives the urban marker from that RUCC;
:post_load_reconciliation;
:publish_provider
renameCollection(dropTarget) swaps
Provider_staging_v_N into place;
:PipelinePublicHealthData.Provider_v_N
PipelinePublicHealthData.SpecialtyMetaData_v_N|
note right
  Every pipeline step writes here and nowhere else.
  No pipeline code holds a credential for the
  serving cluster, so it cannot reach it at all.
end note

|#e5e7eb|Release — a person decides|
:operator runs migrate_data.py naming one collection;
:a browser page opens and blocks
until APPROVE or REJECT is clicked;
if (approved?) then (no)
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:the release is written to
ChatHealthyFrontEnd.pipelineAdmin.Authorizations
as type=data_migration with approval, human_click
and the collection name;
:a webhook starts the migration runbook
in ChatHealthyJobManager;
:the runbook re-reads that record and refuses
unless type, approval, human_click and collection
all match what it was asked to move;
note right
  The click is looked up, never taken on the caller's
  word. Anyone who could reach the webhook could
  otherwise assert their own approval.
end note

|#f3f4f6|Atlas cluster ChatHealthyDataPipelines|
:data_migration.py reads the source collection
as PipelineToFrontEndPublicDataMigrator;

|#dcfce7|Atlas cluster ChatHealthyFrontEnd|
:insert_many into PublicHealthData under the same name
create-only: it refuses if the destination exists;
note right
  This is the only path between the two clusters,
  and the migrator holds no update, no delete and
  no drop on either. A fault here can add data and
  can never alter what is already serving people.
end note
:PublicHealthData.Provider_v_N
PublicHealthData.SpecialtyMetaData_v_N|

|FindCare|
:runtime_data_collections reads
ChatHealthyConfig.DBVersions to learn which
version this environment serves;
fork
  :SpecialtyFilter runs $vectorSearch
on specialty_vector_index;
fork again
  :FindCareService runs find and aggregate
over the Provider collection;
end fork
:results returned to SharedServices;

|Browser|
:ClientRouter posts to /gate
and renders what comes back;
stop

@enduml
